3
00:00:04,478 --> 00:00:05,583
What nobody knew…

4
00:00:05,613 --> 00:00:06,799
was how to get back.

5
00:00:07,222 --> 00:00:08,076
The culprit:

6
00:00:08,162 --> 00:00:08,924
the wind.

7
00:00:09,053 --> 00:00:11,455
In the tropics, the trade winds always

8
00:00:11,266 --> 00:00:12,143
blow west.

9
00:00:12,275 --> 00:00:14,253
Sailing back that way was like walking

10
00:00:14,064 --> 00:00:15,296
up a down escalator.

11
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:18,247
For more than forty years, everyone who

12
00:00:18,058 --> 00:00:19,152
tried it failed.

13
00:00:19,582 --> 00:00:23,566
Until 1565, when the friar Andrés de Urdaneta

14
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:25,046
did something that seemed absurd:

15
00:00:25,236 --> 00:00:27,385
to go east, he headed north.

16
00:00:27,802 --> 00:00:30,456
He climbed to the 39th parallel, level

17
00:00:30,268 --> 00:00:31,144
